\details{
The features of a module can be given as:
\itemize{
\item A comma-separated string (e.g. \code{"HAVCR2,ENTPD1,LAYN,LAG3"}), treated as a
single expression program.
\item A character vector, also a single expression program.
\item A list of character vectors, i.e. multiple programs. When the list is
fully named, the names are used as the metadata column names of the scores
(each program gets its own column, prefixed by the module key), e.g.
\code{list(Exhaustion = c("HAVCR2", "ENTPD1"), Activation = c("IFNG", "GZMB"))}
will add \verb{\{module key\}_Exhaustion} and \verb{\{module key\}_Activation} columns to
the metadata. If the list is not named, the columns will be named
\verb{\{module key\}1}, \verb{\{module key\}2}, etc. A single unnamed program will be
named by the module key. Use one of the reserved keys \verb{_}, \code{-}, \code{*} or \verb{#}
as the module key to skip the prefix.
}

For cell cycle scoring, use \code{"cc.genes"} or \code{"cc.genes.updated.2019"}
(human) or \code{"cc.genes.mouse"} as the features, or set \code{kind} to \code{"cc"}
(with \code{features} defaulting to \code{"cc.genes"}). Then \verb{\{module key\}_S.Score},
\verb{\{module key\}_G2M.Score} and \verb{\{module key\}_Phase} columns will be added to
the metadata (without the prefix when the module key is one of the reserved
no-prefix keys \verb{_}, \code{-}, \code{*} or \verb{#}).

A module can also perform diffusion map (diffusion components) as a
reduction by setting \code{kind} to \code{"dm"}, \code{"diffmap"} or \code{"diffusion_map"}.
In this case, \code{features} is the number of components to keep (default 2),
the first \code{features} components will be added to the metadata as
\verb{\{module key\}_1}, \verb{\{module key\}_2}, ..., and a reduction named
\verb{\{module key\}} will be created. The diffusion map is calculated by
\code{destiny::DiffusionMap()} (see
\url{https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/destiny.html}),
neither Seurat nor UCell is used. Other key-value pairs of the module will
be passed to \code{destiny::DiffusionMap()}.

The parameters (\code{method}, \code{nbin}, \code{ctrl}, \code{k}, \code{assay}, \code{seed}, \code{search}
and those in \code{...}) are the defaults inherited by all modules. They can be
overridden per module by putting the same keys in the module dict.
Irrelevant parameters for a tool are ignored, e.g. \code{nbin} and \code{ctrl} are
only used by \code{Seurat::AddModuleScore()}, and \code{maxRank} is only used by UCell.

Note that the scores from different methods are NOT comparable with each
other (only the column names are consistent). Also, UCell imputes missing
genes with 0 while other methods drop them (with a warning from Seurat).
The \code{slot} parameter of UCell is \code{slot} (not \code{layer}), while other
matrix-based tools (AUCell, ssGSEA, JASMINE, SCSE) read the expression data
from the \code{data} layer (or the layer specified by \code{layer}).
